Release 0.1.2.

Changelog: 17-10-2026 13:10:58

Fixed. The app's folder in the suite is apps/vita3k (was apps/vita3k-manager) and its package is vita3k_manager
(was bc250_vita3k_manager): the suite's naming convention (owner, 17-10-2026), a short folder name and the package
named after the app without the BC-250 prefix; both names are the owner's. With the folder go its key in the
portal, its chapter of the wiki (apps/vita3k/, which the Manual link opens), its installer test and its release
tags: vita3k-v<x.y.z> from the next release on, which the app's update check follows. The installed app keeps its
name, its launcher bc250-vita3k-manager, the run wrapper bc250-vita3k-run that the Steam shortcuts start, its folder
under ~/.local/share with the installed Vita3K, and its settings; the portal moves its record of the installed copy
to the new key.

